The policy includes five strategic guidelines and 13 objectives, with 97 actions and 150 indicators, involving 21 public entities alongside private sector and civil society actors.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2021-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_23', ARRAY['sdg8', 'sdg10', 'peru', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'mandatory', 'sdg6', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'sdg9']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('53ffafa5-5303-57fb-8b38-f60654597781', 'Peru Companies Law Collective Benefit and Interest (BIC)', 'Companies Law Collective Benefit and Interest (BIC)', 'The Law of the Collective Benefit and Interest Company (BIC Company) establishes a regulatory legal framework for this type of company that, in accordance with the Law, refers to the positive material impact or the reduction of a negative impact on society and the environment.', 'The Law of the Collective Benefit and Interest Company (BIC Company) establishes a regulatory legal framework for this type of company that, in accordance with the Law, refers to the positive material impact or the reduction of a negative impact on society and the environment.', 'The Law of the Collective Benefit and Interest Company (BIC Company) establishes a regulatory legal framework for this type of company that, in accordance with the Law, refers to the positive material impact or the reduction of a negative impact on society and the environment.', 'Peru', 'governance', 'in_force', '2018-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_2', ARRAY['mandatory', 'other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('d941509c-788f-55c5-b92b-92a112f6d4f0', 'Peru User Guide for the Preparation of Sustainability Reports', 'User Guide for the Preparation of Sustainability Reports in the Framework of SMV Resolution No. 033-2015-SMV/01', 'This document is a guide to assist in the preparation of the Corporate Sustainability Report approved by SMV Resolution No. 033-2015-SMV/01, which must be submitted by issuers with securities registered in the Public Registry of the Securities Market.', 'This document is a guide to assist in the preparation of the Corporate Sustainability Report approved by SMV Resolution No. 033-2015-SMV/01, which must be submitted by issuers with securities registered in the Public Registry of the Securities Market.', 'This document is a guide to assist in the preparation of the Corporate Sustainability Report approved by SMV Resolution No. 033-2015-SMV/01, which must be submitted by issuers with securities registered in the Public Registry of the Securities Market.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2017-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_7', ARRAY['sdg13', 'peru', 'voluntary', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'voluntary_frameworks']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('d69b70a3-c75a-5fb8-9607-fa9d6ede2b37', 'Peru SMV resolution SMV/01', 'SMV resolution No 033-2015-SMV/01', 'The information presented in this document refers to the actions and standards implemented by the Company in relation to its economic impact, on the environment and social development, corresponding to the fiscal year ending on December 31 of the calendar year prior to its submission, for which Any reference to "the exercise" must be understood as the period indicated above, and is sent as an annex to the Annual Report of the Company under the electronic formats that the Superintendence of the Securities Market (SMV) establishes to facilitate the submission of the information of the present report through the MVnet System.', 'The information presented in this document refers to the actions and standards implemented by the Company in relation to its economic impact, on the environment and social development, corresponding to the fiscal year ending on December 31 of the calendar year prior to its submission, for which Any reference to "the exercise" must be understood as the period indicated above, and is sent as an annex to the Annual Report of the Company under the electronic formats that the Superintendence of the Securities Market (SMV) establishes to facilitate the submission of the information of the present report through the MVnet System.', 'The information presented in this document refers to the actions and standards implemented by the Company in relation to its economic impact, on the environment and social development, corresponding to the fiscal year ending on December 31 of the calendar year prior to its submission, for which Any reference to "the exercise" must be understood as the period indicated above, and is sent as an annex to the Annual Report of the Company under the electronic formats that the Superintendence of the Securities Market (SMV) establishes to facilitate the submission of the information of the present report through the MVnet System.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2015-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_1', ARRAY['regulations', 'mandatory', 'peru', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('0ba84167-b1c0-5e63-a724-ba3de2c60039', 'Peru Resolution S.B.S. Nº 1928-2015 The Superintendent of Banking', 'Resolution S.B.S. Nº 1928-2015 The Superintendent of Banking, Insurance and Private Administrators of Pension Funds', 'The superintendency has set forth the minimum requirements for social and environmental risk management in order to promote these practices among financial firms, and therefore diminish the likelihood and severity of social conflicts associated with business activities to which financial firms allocate capital. The objective of this regulation is to establish minimal requirements for social an environmental risk management in order to encourage the firms to implement the best practices and prudent decision making process. This regulation does not attempt to transfer the responsibility or roles that belong to public institutions in charge of social and environmental issues to the firms, or make the firms responsible for potential regulatory breaches by projects and/or their primary suppliers.', 'The superintendency has set forth the minimum requirements for social and environmental risk management in order to promote these practices among financial firms, and therefore diminish the likelihood and severity of social conflicts associated with business activities to which financial firms allocate capital. The objective of this regulation is to establish minimal requirements for social an environmental risk management in order to encourage the firms to implement the best practices and prudent decision making process. This regulation does not attempt to transfer the responsibility or roles that belong to public institutions in charge of social and environmental issues to the firms, or make the firms responsible for potential regulatory breaches by projects and/or their primary suppliers.', 'The superintendency has set forth the minimum requirements for social and environmental risk management in order to promote these practices among financial firms, and therefore diminish the likelihood and severity of social conflicts associated with business activities to which financial firms allocate capital. The objective of this regulation is to establish minimal requirements for social an environmental risk management in order to encourage the firms to implement the best practices and prudent decision making process. This regulation does not attempt to transfer the responsibility or roles that belong to public institutions in charge of social and environmental issues to the firms, or make the firms responsible for potential regulatory breaches by projects and/or their primary suppliers.', 'Peru', 'governance', 'in_force', '2015-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_15', ARRAY['regulations', 'mandatory', 'peru', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('a2909d91-fa42-5b4b-899f-ada4880ffae2', 'Peru Supreme Decree MINAM. They modify the National Environmental', 'Supreme Decree No. 015-2015-MINAM. They modify the National Environmental Quality Standards for Water and establish complementary provisions for their application', 'The implementation of the technical code for sustainable constructions (CTCS) is an engagement made during the COP20 in Lima, that aims to regulate the technical criteria for the design and construction of sustainable cities and buildings by making efficient use of resources, and reducing GHG emissions. The technical code establishes specific technical requirements when it comes to the rational use of water, energy and refrigeration, emphasizing the use of materials that support the climate conditions where new buildings will be placed.', 'The implementation of the technical code for sustainable constructions (CTCS) is an engagement made during the COP20 in Lima, that aims to regulate the technical criteria for the design and construction of sustainable cities and buildings by making efficient use of resources, and reducing GHG emissions. The technical code establishes specific technical requirements when it comes to the rational use of water, energy and refrigeration, emphasizing the use of materials that support the climate conditions where new buildings will be placed.', 'The implementation of the technical code for sustainable constructions (CTCS) is an engagement made during the COP20 in Lima, that aims to regulate the technical criteria for the design and construction of sustainable cities and buildings by making efficient use of resources, and reducing GHG emissions. The technical code establishes specific technical requirements when it comes to the rational use of water, energy and refrigeration, emphasizing the use of materials that support the climate conditions where new buildings will be placed.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2015-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_19', ARRAY['sdg13', 'other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'sdg11', 'mandatory', 'sdg6']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('f412fceb-a854-53c7-a894-0e2fcdce00c1', 'Peru Protection and Management Regulation Environmental for the Activities', 'Protection and Management Regulation Environmental for the Activities of Exploitation, Benefit, General Labor, Mining Transport and Storage', 'The purpose of this regulation is to ensure that mining activities in the national territory are carried out safeguarding the constitutional right to enjoy a balanced and adequate environment for the development of life, within the framework of free private initiative and the sustainable use of natural resources.', 'The purpose of this regulation is to ensure that mining activities in the national territory are carried out safeguarding the constitutional right to enjoy a balanced and adequate environment for the development of life, within the framework of free private initiative and the sustainable use of natural resources.', 'The purpose of this regulation is to ensure that mining activities in the national territory are carried out safeguarding the constitutional right to enjoy a balanced and adequate environment for the development of life, within the framework of free private initiative and the sustainable use of natural resources.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2014-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_10', ARRAY['other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations', 'sdg11', 'mandatory']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('cff0db8c-044f-51e9-a8bf-cac2fabb28a9', 'Registry of Emissions and Transfer of Pollutants PRTR Peru', 'Registry of Emissions and Transfer of Pollutants PRTR Peru', 'The Registry of Emissions and Transfer of Pollutants RETC Peru, is constituted in an environmental management mechanism that facilitates access to information on releases to the environment of potentially dangerous substances and materials to the citizen; also serving as an input to support policy decisions regarding the management of chemicals as well as their associated risks. This publication details the central elements that should guide the implementation process of the Registry in the country.', 'The Registry of Emissions and Transfer of Pollutants RETC Peru, is constituted in an environmental management mechanism that facilitates access to information on releases to the environment of potentially dangerous substances and materials to the citizen; also serving as an input to support policy decisions regarding the management of chemicals as well as their associated risks. This publication details the central elements that should guide the implementation process of the Registry in the country.', 'The Registry of Emissions and Transfer of Pollutants RETC Peru, is constituted in an environmental management mechanism that facilitates access to information on releases to the environment of potentially dangerous substances and materials to the citizen; also serving as an input to support policy decisions regarding the management of chemicals as well as their associated risks. This publication details the central elements that should guide the implementation process of the Registry in the country.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2014-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_11', ARRAY['sdg13', 'other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'mandatory', 'mandatory_regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('2617f2c7-4b79-5ab5-b57e-faedde7746bf', 'Peru Supreme Decree EM.- Environmental Protection and Management Regulations', 'Supreme Decree No. 040-2014-EM.- Environmental Protection and Management Regulations for Mining Exploitation, Beneficiation, General Labor, Transport and Storage Activities', 'The Environmental Protection Regulation for the Exploitation, Benefit, Transport and Storage of Mining Activities is intended to ensure that mining activities safeguard the constitutional right to enjoy a balanced environment, that supports development. Organizations involved in mining activities will disclose a sustainability report, which contains a record of all the physical, biological, chemical, socioeconomic and landscape components of their project activities, identifying sources of pollution that might have an impact in the areas of influence of the mining project. This report shall be submitted to the Ministry of Energy and Mining and the OEFA in physical and digital format and will be available for public use in the web pages of those organizations.', 'The Environmental Protection Regulation for the Exploitation, Benefit, Transport and Storage of Mining Activities is intended to ensure that mining activities safeguard the constitutional right to enjoy a balanced environment, that supports development. Organizations involved in mining activities will disclose a sustainability report, which contains a record of all the physical, biological, chemical, socioeconomic and landscape components of their project activities, identifying sources of pollution that might have an impact in the areas of influence of the mining project. This report shall be submitted to the Ministry of Energy and Mining and the OEFA in physical and digital format and will be available for public use in the web pages of those organizations.', 'The Environmental Protection Regulation for the Exploitation, Benefit, Transport and Storage of Mining Activities is intended to ensure that mining activities safeguard the constitutional right to enjoy a balanced environment, that supports development. Organizations involved in mining activities will disclose a sustainability report, which contains a record of all the physical, biological, chemical, socioeconomic and landscape components of their project activities, identifying sources of pollution that might have an impact in the areas of influence of the mining project. This report shall be submitted to the Ministry of Energy and Mining and the OEFA in physical and digital format and will be available for public use in the web pages of those organizations.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2014-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_20', ARRAY['peru', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'sdg11', 'mandatory', 'disclosure', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('87e36d36-90c6-5644-bc0a-b09ca78e5c26', 'Code of Good Corporate Governance for Peruvian Companies', 'Code of Good Corporate Governance for Peruvian Companies', 'The Code is aimed at providing an updated version that includes the best standards of good corporate governance identified at the global and local levels, applicable to the Peruvian reality, placing special emphasis on the new advances experienced in this field, especially in the dynamics of the General Meeting of Shareholders (ownership), the Board of Directors (administration) and Senior Management (ordinary management), as well as in the implementation of adequate risk management; all with the aim of promoting the establishment of reciprocal controls and that societies function efficiently.', 'The Code is aimed at providing an updated version that includes the best standards of good corporate governance identified at the global and local levels, applicable to the Peruvian reality, placing special emphasis on the new advances experienced in this field, especially in the dynamics of the General Meeting of Shareholders (ownership), the Board of Directors (administration) and Senior Management (ordinary management), as well as in the implementation of adequate risk management; all with the aim of promoting the establishment of reciprocal controls and that societies function efficiently.', 'The Code is aimed at providing an updated version that includes the best standards of good corporate governance identified at the global and local levels, applicable to the Peruvian reality, placing special emphasis on the new advances experienced in this field, especially in the dynamics of the General Meeting of Shareholders (ownership), the Board of Directors (administration) and Senior Management (ordinary management), as well as in the implementation of adequate risk management; all with the aim of promoting the establishment of reciprocal controls and that societies function efficiently.', 'Peru', 'governance', 'in_force', '2013-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_3', ARRAY['peru', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('80de3016-d63b-5206-849f-ff25e5401e68', 'Peru Law 29783 on Safety and Health at Work', 'Law 29783 on Safety and Health at Work', 'Law No. 29783 on Health and Safety at work, aims to promote a preventive risk culture in the country, that involves employees, employers, the State, and Trade Union organizations. Employers must produce a management report which contains policies and objectives related to health and safety at work, internal regulations (when employers have more than 20 employees), risk assessments, preventive activities and an annual program. Additionally, employers must comply with the mandatory records of the management system of health and safety, this information should also be sent to the National Council of Health and Safety.', 'Law No. 29783 on Health and Safety at work, aims to promote a preventive risk culture in the country, that involves employees, employers, the State, and Trade Union organizations. Employers must produce a management report which contains policies and objectives related to health and safety at work, internal regulations (when employers have more than 20 employees), risk assessments, preventive activities and an annual program. Additionally, employers must comply with the mandatory records of the management system of health and safety, this information should also be sent to the National Council of Health and Safety.', 'Law No. 29783 on Health and Safety at work, aims to promote a preventive risk culture in the country, that involves employees, employers, the State, and Trade Union organizations. Employers must produce a management report which contains policies and objectives related to health and safety at work, internal regulations (when employers have more than 20 employees), risk assessments, preventive activities and an annual program. Additionally, employers must comply with the mandatory records of the management system of health and safety, this information should also be sent to the National Council of Health and Safety.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2012-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_22', ARRAY['sdg8', 'peru', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'disclosure', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('6bddc18a-f99b-577b-9ddc-3512c47e9196', 'Peru National System Law of Evaluation of Environmental Impact', 'National System Law of Evaluation of Environmental Impact and its Regulation', 'The purpose of this Law is: The creation of the National Environmental Impact Assessment System (SEIA), as a single and coordinated system of identification, prevention, supervision, control and early correction of the negative environmental impacts derived from human actions expressed through the investment project. The establishment of a uniform process that includes the requirements, stages, and scope of environmental impact assessments of investment projects. The establishment of mechanisms that ensure citizen participation in the environmental impact assessment process.', 'The purpose of this Law is: The creation of the National Environmental Impact Assessment System (SEIA), as a single and coordinated system of identification, prevention, supervision, control and early correction of the negative environmental impacts derived from human actions expressed through the investment project. The establishment of a uniform process that includes the requirements, stages, and scope of environmental impact assessments of investment projects. The establishment of mechanisms that ensure citizen participation in the environmental impact assessment process.', 'The purpose of this Law is: The creation of the National Environmental Impact Assessment System (SEIA), as a single and coordinated system of identification, prevention, supervision, control and early correction of the negative environmental impacts derived from human actions expressed through the investment project. The establishment of a uniform process that includes the requirements, stages, and scope of environmental impact assessments of investment projects. The establishment of mechanisms that ensure citizen participation in the environmental impact assessment process.', 'Peru', 'governance', 'in_force', '2011-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_9', ARRAY['mandatory', 'other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('32da1a7c-c0d9-585a-b5cc-8ef60310cb5f', 'Peru Labor and employment promotion dictate provisions relating', 'Labor and employment promotion dictate provisions relating to the obligation of employers and medical care centers to report to the ministry work accidents, dangerous incidents and occupational diseases. Supreme Decree No. 012-2010-TR', 'The purpose of this regulation is to encourage employers from all sectors and medical care centers (public, private, military, police or social security) to report to the Ministry of Labor and Employment occupational accidents, dangerous incidents and occupational diseases at work. Within the deadlines and terms established in the Article No. 2 of this regulation, they shall notify through an electronic form available in the system (Information System of Accidents at work, Dangerous incidents and occupational Diseases). This information must be in line with the Supreme Decree No. 009-2005-TR, Article No. 75 and 77 of Regulation of Health and Safety.', 'The purpose of this regulation is to encourage employers from all sectors and medical care centers (public, private, military, police or social security) to report to the Ministry of Labor and Employment occupational accidents, dangerous incidents and occupational diseases at work. Within the deadlines and terms established in the Article No. 2 of this regulation, they shall notify through an electronic form available in the system (Information System of Accidents at work, Dangerous incidents and occupational Diseases). This information must be in line with the Supreme Decree No. 009-2005-TR, Article No. 75 and 77 of Regulation of Health and Safety.', 'The purpose of this regulation is to encourage employers from all sectors and medical care centers (public, private, military, police or social security) to report to the Ministry of Labor and Employment occupational accidents, dangerous incidents and occupational diseases at work. Within the deadlines and terms established in the Article No. 2 of this regulation, they shall notify through an electronic form available in the system (Information System of Accidents at work, Dangerous incidents and occupational Diseases). This information must be in line with the Supreme Decree No. 009-2005-TR, Article No. 75 and 77 of Regulation of Health and Safety.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2010-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_16', ARRAY['sdg8', 'sdg14', 'other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('4997fa3b-254c-5e9d-96d6-345e7b92feda', 'Peru Work and employment promotion dictate provisions regarding the', 'Work and employment promotion dictate provisions regarding the obligation of employers and medical care centers to report to the ministry work accidents, dangerous incidents and occupational diseases Supreme Decree No. 012-2010-tr', 'This document includes provisions related to the obligation of employers and medical centers to report accidents to the ministry work, dangerous incidents and occupational illnesses.', 'This document includes provisions related to the obligation of employers and medical centers to report accidents to the ministry work, dangerous incidents and occupational illnesses.', 'This document includes provisions related to the obligation of employers and medical centers to report accidents to the ministry work, dangerous incidents and occupational illnesses.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2010-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_8', ARRAY['sdg8', 'sdg14', 'other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('518dedc2-909c-547a-a818-93505394d223', 'Peru Supreme Decree MINAM. Approving the national environmental quality', 'Supreme Decree No. 002-2008-MINAM. Approving the national environmental quality standards for water', 'The National Standards for Environmental Quality of Water were approved with the purpose to establish physical, chemical or biological conditions, that do not pose a risk to health, people or the environment.', 'The National Standards for Environmental Quality of Water were approved with the purpose to establish physical, chemical or biological conditions, that do not pose a risk to health, people or the environment.', 'The National Standards for Environmental Quality of Water were approved with the purpose to establish physical, chemical or biological conditions, that do not pose a risk to health, people or the environment.', 'Peru', 'governance', 'in_force', '2008-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_17', ARRAY['other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg6', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('03f057ed-d774-532e-be9a-4b37e71a8cba', 'Peru Supreme Decree TR approving the Occupational Health', 'Supreme Decree no. 009-2005-TR approving the Occupational Health and Safety Regulations', 'The purpose of this regulation is to establish rules and guidelines for the prevention of risks at work. It applies to employees, employers and the State, who through social dialogue, will ensure the promotion, dissemination and enforcement on the matter. In the case of any occupational accident, dangerous incident or occupational diseases at work, employers and medical care centers shall notify to the competent authority using the electronic form No.1, No. 2, and No.4, indicated in the relevant annexes of this regulation.', 'The purpose of this regulation is to establish rules and guidelines for the prevention of risks at work. It applies to employees, employers and the State, who through social dialogue, will ensure the promotion, dissemination and enforcement on the matter. In the case of any occupational accident, dangerous incident or occupational diseases at work, employers and medical care centers shall notify to the competent authority using the electronic form No.1, No. 2, and No.4, indicated in the relevant annexes of this regulation.', 'The purpose of this regulation is to establish rules and guidelines for the prevention of risks at work. It applies to employees, employers and the State, who through social dialogue, will ensure the promotion, dissemination and enforcement on the matter. In the case of any occupational accident, dangerous incident or occupational diseases at work, employers and medical care centers shall notify to the competent authority using the electronic form No.1, No. 2, and No.4, indicated in the relevant annexes of this regulation.', 'Peru', 'nature', 'in_force', '2005-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_18', ARRAY['sdg8', 'sdg14', 'other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('f6613ba0-f5a6-51e1-9d48-6b62562acdcb', 'Peru Approval of the Regulations of Law , General', 'Approval of the Regulations of Law No. 27314, General Law on Solid Waste SUPREME DECREE No. 057-2004-PCM', 'This regulation aims to ensure the appropriate management of solid waste to prevent health risks, protect and promote environmental quality and the welfare of citizens. It sets out specific requirements for the mining waste generators according to Art. 36. In addition,   solid waste management companies (EPS-RS & EC-RS), and the district and regional municipalities that are directly providing solid waste services must submit to the health authority within their jurisdiction, their operator report detailing the waste managed during last month, using the form indicated in Annex 3 of this regulation.', 'This regulation aims to ensure the appropriate management of solid waste to prevent health risks, protect and promote environmental quality and the welfare of citizens. It sets out specific requirements for the mining waste generators according to Art. 36. In addition,   solid waste management companies (EPS-RS & EC-RS), and the district and regional municipalities that are directly providing solid waste services must submit to the health authority within their jurisdiction, their operator report detailing the waste managed during last month, using the form indicated in Annex 3 of this regulation.', 'This regulation aims to ensure the appropriate management of solid waste to prevent health risks, protect and promote environmental quality and the welfare of citizens. It sets out specific requirements for the mining waste generators according to Art. 36. In addition,   solid waste management companies (EPS-RS & EC-RS), and the district and regional municipalities that are directly providing solid waste services must submit to the health authority within their jurisdiction, their operator report detailing the waste managed during last month, using the form indicated in Annex 3 of this regulation.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2004-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_21', ARRAY['other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations', 'sdg11', 'mandatory', 'sdg12', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('5672de29-21cb-5535-a756-49aa1eb961cc', 'Principles of Good Governance for Peruvian Companies', 'Principles of Good Governance for Peruvian Companies', 'The corporate governance structure specifies the distribution of rights and responsibilities among different participants in the corporation, such as, the board, managers, shareholders and other stakeholders, and spells out the rules and procedures for making decisions on corporate affairs.', 'The corporate governance structure specifies the distribution of rights and responsibilities among different participants in the corporation, such as, the board, managers, shareholders and other stakeholders, and spells out the rules and procedures for making decisions on corporate affairs.', 'The corporate governance structure specifies the distribution of rights and responsibilities among different participants in the corporation, such as, the board, managers, shareholders and other stakeholders, and spells out the rules and procedures for making decisions on corporate affairs.', 'Peru', 'governance', 'in_force', '2002-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_5', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'peru', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('31e64118-d25e-59af-84f6-3f464f255b69', 'Peru Law , Law of the National Environmental Impact', 'Law No. 27446, Law of the National Environmental Impact Assessment System and this Regulation', 'The National System of Environmental Impact Evaluation (SEIA), constitutes a unique and coordinated system to identify, prevent, supervise and control in advance negative environmental impact arising from investment projects. Relevant subjects before they start their activities and operations must follow a process of environmental certification. This will involve, describing the proposed action and the background, identifying direct and indirect environmental impacts during the project, environmental risks, goals, community involvement, monitoring and control plans and an economic assessment of environmental impact.', 'The National System of Environmental Impact Evaluation (SEIA), constitutes a unique and coordinated system to identify, prevent, supervise and control in advance negative environmental impact arising from investment projects. Relevant subjects before they start their activities and operations must follow a process of environmental certification. This will involve, describing the proposed action and the background, identifying direct and indirect environmental impacts during the project, environmental risks, goals, community involvement, monitoring and control plans and an economic assessment of environmental impact.', 'The National System of Environmental Impact Evaluation (SEIA), constitutes a unique and coordinated system to identify, prevent, supervise and control in advance negative environmental impact arising from investment projects. Relevant subjects before they start their activities and operations must follow a process of environmental certification. This will involve, describing the proposed action and the background, identifying direct and indirect environmental impacts during the project, environmental risks, goals, community involvement, monitoring and control plans and an economic assessment of environmental impact.', 'Peru', 'governance', 'in_force', '2001-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_14', ARRAY['peru', 'regulations', 'sdg11', 'mandatory', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('b3549117-42f1-57b7-b5d1-5b3d895e400c', 'Peru: Code of Good Corporate Governance for Companies', 'Peru: Code of Good Corporate Governance for Companies Securities Issuers', 'This document outlines the Code of Good Corporate Governance for Companies Securities Issuers. It was published in 2001.', 'This document outlines the Code of Good Corporate Governance for Companies Securities Issuers. It was published in 2001.', 'This document outlines the Code of Good Corporate Governance for Companies Securities Issuers. It was published in 2001.', 'Peru', 'governance', 'in_force', '2001-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_4', ARRAY['peru', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('c8775a70-9a48-5172-90c0-157665c1ce3b', 'Peru Law .- General Law on Solid Waste', 'Law No. 27314.- General Law on Solid Waste', 'This law establishes the rights, duties and responsibilities of individual and legal person within national territory to ensure an appropriate and environmental management of solid waste. In this sense, sectors such as health, environment and development are linked to achieve an integrated approach to waste management. Under this law, solid waste management companies (EPS-RS & EC-RS) and municipalities, the ''Operators'', that directly provide solid waste management services must submit quarterly reports to specialized technical units in environmental health in the Ministry of Health, describing the system applied to the management of solid waste including characteristics of solid waste in terms of quantity, risks, operations and processes.', 'This law establishes the rights, duties and responsibilities of individual and legal person within national territory to ensure an appropriate and environmental management of solid waste. In this sense, sectors such as health, environment and development are linked to achieve an integrated approach to waste management. Under this law, solid waste management companies (EPS-RS & EC-RS) and municipalities, the ''Operators'', that directly provide solid waste management services must submit quarterly reports to specialized technical units in environmental health in the Ministry of Health, describing the system applied to the management of solid waste including characteristics of solid waste in terms of quantity, risks, operations and processes.', 'This law establishes the rights, duties and responsibilities of individual and legal person within national territory to ensure an appropriate and environmental management of solid waste. In this sense, sectors such as health, environment and development are linked to achieve an integrated approach to waste management. Under this law, solid waste management companies (EPS-RS & EC-RS) and municipalities, the ''Operators'', that directly provide solid waste management services must submit quarterly reports to specialized technical units in environmental health in the Ministry of Health, describing the system applied to the management of solid waste including characteristics of solid waste in terms of quantity, risks, operations and processes.', 'Peru', 'climate', 'in_force', '2000-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_13', ARRAY['other sustainability policy', 'peru', 'regulations', 'sdg11', 'mandatory', 'sdg12', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('066604b9-a306-5afe-aa4a-dc9e85fc0379', 'Peru Corporations Act Law', 'Corporations Act Law No. 26887', 'Corporate governance in Peru is specifically regulated in a wide range of legislation covering various areas of specialization. The General Law on Corporations (Law 26887), regulates the organization of companies, ownership of shares and executive and management entities (general assembly of shareholders, board of governors and management), establishes the corresponding responsibilities, describes shareholder rights and obligations and sets guidelines on the sale of shares and the merger, acquisition and demerger of companies.', 'Corporate governance in Peru is specifically regulated in a wide range of legislation covering various areas of specialization. The General Law on Corporations (Law 26887), regulates the organization of companies, ownership of shares and executive and management entities (general assembly of shareholders, board of governors and management), establishes the corresponding responsibilities, describes shareholder rights and obligations and sets guidelines on the sale of shares and the merger, acquisition and demerger of companies.', 'Corporate governance in Peru is specifically regulated in a wide range of legislation covering various areas of specialization. The General Law on Corporations (Law 26887), regulates the organization of companies, ownership of shares and executive and management entities (general assembly of shareholders, board of governors and management), establishes the corresponding responsibilities, describes shareholder rights and obligations and sets guidelines on the sale of shares and the merger, acquisition and demerger of companies.', 'Peru', 'governance', 'in_force', '1997-01-01'::date, 'Peru', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/143_12', ARRAY['peru', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('e5c0c085-29c3-5841-8c02-65d26ab10339', 'Philippines Sustainable Finance Framework - Circular', 'Sustainable Finance Framework - Circular No. 1085', 'The guidance requires banks to embed sustainability principles (including those covering environmental and social risk areas) in their corporate governance framework, risk management systems and strategic objectives consistent with their size, risk profile and complexity of operations. Banks are provided a period of 3 years within which to fully comply, however shall provides a board-approved transition plan upon request of the BSP starting six months from the effectivity of the circular''s issuance.', 'The guidance requires banks to embed sustainability principles (including those covering environmental and social risk areas) in their corporate governance framework, risk management systems and strategic objectives consistent with their size, risk profile and complexity of operations. Banks are provided a period of 3 years within which to fully comply, however shall provides a board-approved transition plan upon request of the BSP starting six months from the effectivity of the circular''s issuance.', 'The guidance requires banks to embed sustainability principles (including those covering environmental and social risk areas) in their corporate governance framework, risk management systems and strategic objectives consistent with their size, risk profile and complexity of operations. Banks are provided a period of 3 years within which to fully comply, however shall provides a board-approved transition plan upon request of the BSP starting six months from the effectivity of the circular''s issuance.', 'Philippines', 'governance', 'in_force', '2021-01-01'::date, 'Philippines', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/144_30', ARRAY['voluntary_frameworks', 'other sustainability policy', 'sdg16', 'philippines', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('c6d00384-4caa-5e75-9590-cff55177e489', 'Philippines Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP) Circular – Sustainable', 'Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP) Circular No. 1085 – Sustainable Finance Framework', 'Issued in April 2020, Circular No. 1085 establishes a Sustainable Finance Framework requiring banks to integrate environmental and social (E&S) risk considerations into their corporate governance and risk management systems. The policy aims to enhance financial stability by addressing the potential impacts of climate change and social risks on the banking sector.

Key provisions include:

Integration of Sustainability Principles: Banks must embed environmental and social (E&S) risk in their governance, risk management, and strategic planning.
Environmental and Social Risk Management System (ESRMS): Financial institutions must implement an ESRMS to assess, monitor, and mitigate E&S risks.
Board and Senior Management Responsibilities:
Boards must approve and oversee sustainability strategies.
Senior management must ensure compliance with risk management policies.
Disclosure and Reporting Requirements:
Annual reports must include sustainability objectives, E&S risk exposures, and climate-related financial disclosures.
Banks issuing green, social, or sustainability bonds must report their alignment with international sustainability standards.
Regulatory Compliance Timeline:
Banks have three years from the Circular’s effectivity to fully comply.
A transition plan with clear timelines must be developed.
The framework aligns with global sustainable finance initiatives and supports the Philippine Development Plan in promoting environmentally and socially responsible financial decisions.', 'Issued in April 2020, Circular No. 1085 establishes a Sustainable Finance Framework requiring banks to integrate environmental and social (E&S) risk considerations into their corporate governance and risk management systems. The policy aims to enhance financial stability by addressing the potential impacts of climate change and social risks on the banking sector.

Key provisions include:

