Banks issuing green, social, or sustainability bonds must report their alignment with international sustainability standards.
Regulatory Compliance Timeline:
Banks have three years from the Circular’s effectivity to fully comply.
A transition plan with clear timelines must be developed.
The framework aligns with global sustainable finance initiatives and supports the Philippine Development Plan in promoting environmentally and socially responsible financial decisions.', 'Issued in April 2020, Circular No. 1085 establishes a Sustainable Finance Framework requiring banks to integrate environmental and social (E&S) risk considerations into their corporate governance and risk management systems. The policy aims to enhance financial stability by addressing the potential impacts of climate change and social risks on the banking sector.

